proxy reads, in co_localsplusnames' order (tbobj.go's frameSlots; queue 219)"] [55 2 "// lineStarts are the instructions that may start a line event, by instruction (trace.go's traceLines; queue 219t)"] [57 2 "// monLocal are the code's local sys.monitoring events by tool (set_local_events, monitoring.go; queue 281), nil for none"] [59 2 "// obj is the code's object (co_* attributes), one per code so that frame.f_code is func.__code__ (queue 219t)"] [61 2 "// parent is the code whose constant this is; imports, on a module's, the names its scope binds by import (queue 229)"] [64 2 "// view is CPython's bytecode of the code, made when asked (bytecode_asm.go)"] [66 26 "// the jumps flow! threaded (the IR's :threaded)"] [68 2 "// cimpl is whether the code is of the Python code that stands for CPython's C (cImplModules; trace.go's inCImpl,"] [69 2 "// queue 293): 0 not known yet, 1 not, 2 it is"] [75 1 "// codePos is an instruction's end line (less its line) and columns (0-based UTF-8 byte offsets), Col -1 when unknown:"] [76 1 "// co_positions' last three items (the first, the line, is Lines')."] [84 1 "// debugRanges is config.code_debug_ranges: false under -X no_debug_ranges or PYTHONNODEBUGRANGES (the code objects then"] [85 1 "// carry no columns: co_positions' None, no caret lines)"] [94 1 "// Position is instruction pc's location as co_positions gives it: line, end line, column, end column, each 0 when"] [95 1 "// unknown (ok false for the columns)."] [113 1 "// decodePositions reads positionsText: per instruction \"COL,END-COL[,END-LINE-LESS-LINE]\" or \"\" (no columns), \";\""] [114 1 "// between them (arbace.python.compile's positions-of). codePos.EndLine holds the end line less the line."] [140 1 "// compileWarning is a SyntaxWarning the compiler made: its message and location (1-based offsets, 0 unknown)."] [146 1 "// NativeFunc is a code object's compiled body (PY8's AOT, aot.go): it runs f from f.PC as step does"] [147 1 "// (the value returned, an error raised, or a *pushFrame for a call of a Python function)."] [150 1 "// CodeKind is the IR's :kind."] [165 1 "// CodeFlags are the IR's :flags."] [176 24 "// CO_ITERABLE_COROUTINE: a generator types.coroutine marked (set at run time, PY5d)"] [179 1 "// Instr is an instruction: the operation and its argument decoded into two integers (§7.2's table:"] [180 1 "// an index, a count, a jump target, an operator, a flag ...)."] [186 1 "// Handler is a row of the exception table: instructions [Start, End) go to Target with the stack"] [187 1 "// popped to Depth, then the instruction's index pushed when Lasti, then the exception."] [193 1 "// Make-function's parts (the IR's [CONST PARTS]), as a bit set in B."] [201 1 "// Intrinsic is the IR's :call-intrinsic NAME (§3.4)."] [222 1 "// Object is c's code object, the same each time (f_code, __code__, gi_code: CPython's one PyCodeObject; queue 219t)."] [230 1 "// handlerAt is the handler covering instruction pc, or nil."] [241 1 "// Line is instruction pc's line, 0 when unknown (-1: none, in a replaced line table)."] [244 3 "// a replaced line table (queue 248): the view's line of the instruction's code unit, -1 for none"] [249 14 "// past the table's end"] [259 1 "// OpNames is the IR's operations the loader knows, in Op order (bin/pyi runtime check compares them"] [260 1 "// with arbace.python.ir/ops)."] [263 1 "// OpOwners is each operation's owner (PYI-SPEC.md §9), in Op order."] [266 1 "// SetFilename sets the code object's co_filename and its nested code objects'."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[106 26] [243 16] [246 29] [270 31]] :go/trails [[219 75]]} (go/file "code.go" :imports [


